Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The PNG and APNG decoder and encoder are original implementations written
from the W3C Portable Network Graphics (PNG) Specification, Third Edition
(which incorporates APNG, cICP, mDCV, cLLI and eXIf). The DEFLATE and zlib
codec is an original implementation written from RFC 1951 (DEFLATE
Compressed Data Format Specification version 1.3) and RFC 1950 (ZLIB
Compressed Data Format Specification version 3.3). They are not translations
of, and do not derive from, any other implementation's source: no code of
libpng, zlib, zlib-ng, miniz, libdeflate, stb_image, lodepng, or of the
png, flate2, miniz_oxide or fdeflate crates was read or consulted. The fixed
tables (DEFLATE's length and distance bases and extra bits, the code length
order, the fixed Huffman code; PNG's Adam7 pass geometry) are reproduced
from those documents.

The decoder is tested against PngSuite by Willem van Schaik (2017-07-19
release, http://www.schaik.com/pngsuite/), whose images are included in
tests/pngsuite under their own terms: "Permission to use, copy, modify and
distribute these images for any purpose and without fee is hereby granted."
(tests/pngsuite/PngSuite.LICENSE). tests/pngsuite/SHA256SUMS records their
source and hashes. They are test data only and are not part of the published
crate.

